_The Economist_ has a special edition of 1993 forecasts which contains
some interesting comments.  Among them is that sovereign countries
will fade in importance.  Their power and/or loyalty will shift to:

* Continental trade & regulation regimes (European Community, 
  NAFTA, CIS, etc.)
* International ethnic networks (English, Chinese, Latinos,
  etc.)
* Multinational corporations 

This gives us three interesting arenas to watch for emerging law over 
the next few years.  

They also note that international trade has expanded 20-fold since 1950,
to $8 trillion.  During 1950-1983 it grew at 3%/year; since 1984 it's
been growing at 6%/year.

