Subject: Outlawry

One non-coercive way to discourage convicted, non-compliant criminals is to
make them "outlaws."  Until they comply with the court's verdict (e.g. make
restitution arrangements)  that court won't be available to protect them;
they're on their own when confronted with theft or assault.  
 
This doesn't imply sanctioning coercion against them, just that if this
happens society won't protect them.  
 
